    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1252" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aenus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-os</span></b> ,
			i, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Αἶνος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city of Thrace</i>, <i>south-east of the</i>
			Palus Stentoris, <i>through which one of the mouths of
				the Hebrus falls into the sea</i>, now <i>Enos</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 2, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 11,
				18, § 43</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Fl.
			14</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 31, 16</span></i> 4.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aenĭi</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Ænus</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 37,
			33</span></i>; <i><span class="en">38, 41</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">45, 27</span></i>. 
			</div>
